From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:20:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: reactions and replies through the transport

* Send and receive message reactions through transport signals

The webOS Messaging app shows reactions as badges on a message, not as
extra text lines. The webOS libpurple transport provides process-wide
signals for this, and this patch talks to them:

- Received: stash each message's server id as "webos-msg-id" on the
  conversation the message is written to, so the transport can store it
  as the serviceMessageId. Turn properties.emotions[] and live
  "reactionInChat" trouter activities into one aggregated
  "webos-im-reaction-set" signal, with emoji in the HTML-entity form the
  app renders. This replaces the "N users reacted with :x:" text.
- Sent: handle "webos-im-send-reaction" for this plugin's accounts and
  PUT (add) or DELETE (remove) {"emotions":{"key":...,"value":<ms>}} on
  .../messages/<id>/properties?name=emotions. teams_post_or_get() now
  attaches the body and Content-Type to a DELETE as well.
- Our own sent messages: emit "webos-im-outbox-id" with the server id
  from the echo, so the user can react to their own messages.

On a libpurple without these signals, purple_signal_connect() returns 0
and nothing is sent, but received reactions are then no longer shown as
text. A version for upstream would need to keep that text when no
listener is connected.

* Show replies as quote cards and send replies with a quote

Teams wraps a reply as an inline
<blockquote itemtype="http://schema.skype.com/Reply" itemid=...> block in
front of the reply body. The webOS Messaging app shows the quoted message
as a card above the reply instead.

- Received: take the leading reply blockquote off the body and stash the
  quoted author, text and message id on the conversation as
  "webos-quoted-from", "webos-quoted-text" and "webos-quoted-id", which
  the webOS transport reads.
- Cache author, time, conversation and plain text of received and own
  messages by server id (at most 400 entries in quote_meta_hash).
- Sent: when the transport stashed "webos-reply-to" on the conversation,
  rebuild the reply blockquote from that cache and put it in front of the
  outgoing message, so other Teams clients show it as a reply.

The conversation data keys belong to the webOS transport, so this is
webOS-only. Making received replies and sending replies work in Pidgin
would need a different UI hook.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
